<title>ESTONIA: EVEA SAYS FEW FUNDS IN FROZEN ACCOUNT.</title>
<headline>EVEA SAYS FEW FUNDS IN FROZEN ACCOUNT.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>EVEA Pank said on Wednesday that it had ordered the closure of its correspondent account with the St Petersburg Promstroibank on July 31 and that it had few funds in it when the city's tax police froze it.</p>
<p>The St Petersburg tax police have frozen the foreign exchange accounts of sevel Estonian banks in two St Petersberg banks saying the owners of the accounts had not complied with tax regulations.</p>
<p>Forekspank has said that it was taking the action of the tax police to court as it said it was unlawful.</p>
<p>-- Tallinn newsroom +372 620 9202 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
